---
source: crates/dyno-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"check\", \"--help\"])"
---
[phase 1] Check a build folder, a launch URL, or every game in a games file

Usage: dyno check [OPTIONS] [TARGET]...

Arguments:
  [TARGET]...
          [phase 1] A build folder or .zip (static scan), an http(s) launch URL (browser run), or one of each

Options:
      --baseline
          [phase 2] Check the empty build inside dyno instead of a target: one page with nothing on it, whose build id never changes. With --device, it gives the phone's footprint with no game

      --games <FILE>
          [phase 1] Check every game in a games file (TOML, or JSON by the .json extension)

      --shard <I/N>
          [phase 1] Check only shard I of N of the games file, such as 1/4

      --budget <FILE>
          [phase 1] The budget file (TOML, or JSON by the .json extension)

      --out <FILE>
          [phase 1] Write the JSON result to FILE instead of stdout

      --host-profile <NAME>
          [phase 1] How the host page embeds the game, and the contract it checks
          
          [default: reels]
          [possible values: reels]

      --game <NAME>
          [phase 1] The game name to label the result with. Outside the result hash

      --release <VERSION>
          [phase 1] The release version to label the result with, such as v12. Outside the result hash

      --game-id <UUID>
          [phase 3] The game's id on the dyno site, a UUID. Default: the entry for the build in the nearest dyno.toml above it. Outside the result hash

      --driver <DRIVER>
          [phase 1] The browser driver: cdp, the built-in Chromium driver; exec:PROGRAM, a program that speaks the runner protocol on stdin and stdout; or serve, which serves the build and waits for a browser on the network to open it, such as Safari on an iPhone. exec needs a launch URL, and serve needs a build folder and no launch URL
          
          [default: cdp]

      --serve-host <HOST>
          [phase 1] With --driver serve, the address a browser reaches this machine at. Default: this machine's address on its local network

      --serve-port <PORT>
          [phase 1] With --driver serve, the harness page's port. The game is on the next one [default: 7370]

      --serve-query <QUERY>
          [phase 1] With --driver serve, the query string the game loads with, such as a demo session's sessionID and rgs_url. No result records it

      --scenario <SCENARIO>
          [phase 2] The harness scenario of the browser run. Any scenario but `alone` needs a launch URL

          Possible values:
          - alone:   [phase 1] The game alone in a fresh harness page
          - aged:    [phase 2] The harness page after 10 earlier games
          - overlap: [phase 2] The game active while the next one preloads
          
          [default: alone]

      --spins <N>
          [phase 2] Play N demo spins after load. Needs a launch URL

      --device
          [phase 2] Also record the game's memory on the connected iPhone with xctrace, while its Safari runs the check. Needs --driver serve and a Mac with Xcode

      --device-id <ID>
          [phase 2] With --device, the device to record, by its UDID or name as `xcrun xctrace list devices` gives them. Default: the only connected iPhone

      --no-open
          [phase 2] With --device, do not open the page in the phone's Safari: open it by hand

      --upload
          [phase 3] Upload the result to the dyno site and print its link, or each game's with --games. Needs dyno login or DYNO_TOKEN

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Exit codes:
  0   pass, or warn
  1   fail: a budget or rule fails
  2   incomplete: a required measure is missing, or a budget or rule could not be checked
  3   invalid: a required measure or an input result failed its own check
  64  usage or config error
  70  internal or I/O error
